oche-Guyon","artist":"Camille Pissarro (French, 1830–1903)","date":"1866","medium":"etching","dimensions":"Image: 27.4 x 22.2 cm (10 13/16 x 8 3/4 in.); Plate: 31.8 x 23.9 cm (12 1/2 x 9 7/16 in.); Sheet: 43.5 x 32.8 cm (17 1/8 x 12 15/16 in.)","culture":"France, 19th century","accession":"1976.20","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1976.20","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/148759","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1976.20/1976.20_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1976.20/1976.20_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"라 로슈기용","description":"라 로슈기용의 커다란 바위를 담은 초기 에칭입니다. 피사로는 새긴 선과 인쇄판 표면에 남은 잉크를 이용해 강한 햇빛과 부드러운 그림자를 구성하며 판화에서도 회화적인 풍경 표현을 시도했습니다.","themes":["풍경과 빛"],"artist_ids":["camille-pissarro"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":687,"image_height":893,"image_bytes":524533,"sha256":"fe19d71ce747aec0de78ec91d1621384b4b884e8333201f85762bb616fdf393b","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"에칭","dimensions_ko":"Image: 27.4 × 22.2 cm; Plate: 31.8 × 23.9 cm; 종이: 43.5 × 32.8 cm"},{"id":"cma-149410","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"In the Waves (Dans les Vagues)","artist":"Paul Gauguin (French, 1848–1903)","date":"1889","medium":"oil on canvas","dimensions":"Framed: 123.8 x 106 x 7 cm (48 3/4 x 41 3/4 x 2 3/4 in.); Unframed: 92.5 x 72.4 cm (36 7/16 x 28 1/2 in.)","culture":"France, 19th century","accession":"1978.63","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1978.63","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/149410","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1978.63/1978.63_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1978.63/1978.63_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"파도 속에서","description":"브르타뉴의 퐁타방에서 제작한, 바다로 몸을 던지는 인물의 그림입니다. 초록과 주황의 강한 대비와 단순화한 윤곽은 관찰한 풍경을 그대로 재현하기보다 상징적인 장면으로 바꿉니다. 1889년 파리의 카페 볼피니에서 전시되었습니다.","themes":["인물과 일상","풍경과 빛"],"artist_ids":["paul-gauguin"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":700,"image_height":900,"image_bytes":267252,"sha256":"7657cab5166c48ad5ad1bbeae52f7f0f627533949fa0d543b4fd249fb58aa0c9","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"캔버스에 유채","dimensions_ko":"액자 포함: 123.8 × 106 × 7 cm; 액자 제외: 92.5 × 72.4 cm"},{"id":"cma-148297","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"The Large Tree","artist":"Paul Gauguin (French, 1848–1903)","date":"1891","medium":"oil on canvas","dimensions":"Framed: 92.4 x 112.7 x 6.4 cm (36 3/8 x 44 3/8 x 2 1/2 in.); Unframed: 74 x 92.8 cm (29 1/8 x 36 9/16 in.)","culture":"France, 19th century","accession":"1975.263","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1975.263","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/148297","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1975.263/1975.263_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1975.263/1975.263_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"큰 나무","description":"고갱이 1891년 타히티에 도착한 뒤 처음 제작한 그림들 가운데 하나입니다. 큰 나무의 그늘 아래 인물들을 띠처럼 배치하고 풍부한 색과 양식화한 형태로 상징적이고 수수께끼 같은 분위기를 만들었습니다.","themes":["인물과 일상","풍경과 빛"],"artist_ids":["paul-gauguin"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":900,"image_height":713,"image_bytes":326097,"sha256":"38dbaae1842a813dcf12a4873740e34143ea1355a42f9ce14ed3fe974d1993e0","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"캔버스에 유채","dimensions_ko":"액자 포함: 92.4 × 112.7 × 6.4 cm; 액자 제외: 74 × 92.8 cm"},{"id":"cma-123168","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"The Call","artist":"Paul Gauguin (French, 1848–1903)","date":"1902","medium":"oil on canvas","dimensions":"Framed: 160.5 x 119 x 9.5 cm (63 3/16 x 46 7/8 x 3 3/4 in.); Unframed: 131.3 x 89.5 cm (51 11/16 x 35 1/4 in.)","culture":"France, late 19th–early 20th century","accession":"1943.392","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1943.392","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/123168","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1943.392/1943.392_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1943.392/1943.392_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"부름","description":"고갱이 죽기 한 해 전 폴리네시아에서 제작한 후기 작품입니다. 맨발의 두 여인 가운데 한 명이 화면 밖을 향해 손짓합니다. 미술관은 이 장면을 삶과 죽음, 운명의 부름을 탐구한 후기 그림들과 연결해 설명합니다.","themes":["인물과 일상"],"artist_ids":["paul-gauguin"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":606,"image_height":900,"image_bytes":233251,"sha256":"3848b74e46adbd5a43b819cb1a6cb63ed2fbae7b20f8d021a9c763131b37fda5","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"캔버스에 유채","dimensions_ko":"액자 포함: 160.5 × 119 × 9.5 cm; 액자 제외: 131.3 × 89.5 cm"},{"id":"cma-127115","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"Head of a Tahitian Woman","artist":"Paul Gauguin (French, 1848–1903)","date":"1891","medium":"graphite with stumping and graphite wash on parchment","dimensions":"Sheet: 30.5 x 24.4 cm (12 x 9 5/8 in.)","culture":"France, 19th century","accession":"1949.439","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1949.439","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/127115","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1949.439/1949.439_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1949.439/1949.439_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"타히티 여인의 얼굴","description":"고갱이 타히티에 도착한 직후 제작한 정교한 초상 드로잉들 가운데 하나입니다. 새로운 장소의 사람과 풍경을 드로잉으로 관찰하던 시기의 작업으로, 세밀한 흑연의 명암이 얼굴의 표정과 입체감을 드러냅니다.","themes":["인물과 일상"],"artist_ids":["paul-gauguin"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":713,"image_height":893,"image_bytes":402678,"sha256":"448e2658eb82a25e127bf26ffd2362c2092f660afb53d32dd96c11722928ab99","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"양피지에 흑연, 문질러 번지는 기법과 흑연 워시","dimensions_ko":"종이: 30.5 × 24.4 cm"},{"id":"cma-114196","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"Nave Nave Fenua (Fragrant Isle)","artist":"Paul Gauguin (French, 1848–1903)","date":"1893–94","medium":"color woodcut","dimensions":"Sheet: 38.5 x 22.8 cm (15 3/16 x 9 in.); Platemark: 35.7 x 20.5 cm (14 1/16 x 8 1/16 in.)","culture":"France, 19th century","accession":"1933.444","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1933.444","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/114196","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1933.444/1933.444_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1933.444/1933.444_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"나베 나베 페누아 — 향기로운 섬","description":"타히티에서의 경험을 설명하려던 삽화 책 《노아 노아》를 위해 만든 목판화입니다. 완성되지 못한 책의 삽화 가운데 하나로, 거칠게 파낸 목판의 흔적이 울창한 풍경과 인물을 구성합니다.","themes":["인물과 일상","풍경과 빛"],"artist_ids":["paul-gauguin"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":525,"image_height":893,"image_bytes":446558,"sha256":"96933abc31f231532e9308b0a95b1be8cedb9aeda9a790ee62c9526fc3d6cceb","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"컬러 목판화","dimensions_ko":"종이: 38.5 × 22.8 cm; 판자국: 35.7 × 20.5 cm"},{"id":"cma-148753","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"Violette Heymann","artist":"Odilon Redon (French, 1840–1916)","date":"1910","medium":"pastel on gray wove paper","dimensions":"Unframed: 72 x 92 cm (28 3/8 x 36 1/4 in.)","culture":"France, early 20th Century","accession":"1926.1976","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1926.1976","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/148753","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1926.1976/1926.1976_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1926.1976/1926.1976_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"비올레트 에만","description":"수집가 마르셀 카프페레르의 어린 조카를 꽃과 함께 그린 파스텔 초상입니다. 흑백 작업에서 풍부한 색채로 옮겨 간 르동의 후기 경향이 드러나며, 인물의 집중한 시선과 주변 꽃이 꿈같은 분위기를 만듭니다.","themes":["인물과 일상","꽃과 사물"],"artist_ids":["odilon-redon"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":900,"image_height":705,"image_bytes":248852,"sha256":"7e2b68c6e300184b24215ca1fb7cb646c87948cf4f257cdd19231e350c4c8e82","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"회색 평직지에 파스텔","dimensions_ko":"액자 제외: 72 × 92 cm"},{"id":"cma-108544","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"Orpheus","artist":"Odilon Redon (French, 1840–1916)","date":"c. 1903–10","medium":"pastel on brown paper","dimensions":"Sheet: 68.8 x 56.8 cm (27 1/16 x 22 3/8 in.)","culture":"France","accession":"1926.25","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1926.25","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/108544","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1926.25/1926.25_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1926.25/1926.25_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"오르페우스","description":"시인이자 음악가 오르페우스의 머리와 그 뒤의 파르나소스산을 밝은 파스텔 층으로 표현했습니다. 르동은 죽음 뒤에도 음악이 이어지는 신화에 관심을 가졌고, 꿈과 정신세계의 주제를 여러 재료로 반복했습니다.","themes":["신화와 상상"],"artist_ids":["odilon-redon"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":744,"image_height":900,"image_bytes":225241,"sha256":"83cc1378994e93dd5a81f1cca2470547920679a693a9a1e12ad9e9dd03567376","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"갈색 종이에 파스텔","dimensions_ko":"종이: 68.8 × 56.8 cm"},{"id":"cma-135469","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"Vase of Flowers","artist":"Odilon Redon (French, 1840–1916)","date":"1916","medium":"pastel","dimensions":"Sheet: 84.1 x 58 cm (33 1/8 x 22 13/16 in.)","culture":"France, 20th century","accession":"1958.46","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1958.46","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/135469","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1958.46/1958.46_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1958.46/1958.46_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"꽃병 — 파스텔","description":"르동이 생애 말기에 집중한 꽃 정물 가운데 하나입니다. 선명한 파스텔 색채와 오래된 정물 주제를 결합한 이 작품은 1939년 뉴욕 세계박람회에 출품되었으며, 현재 클리블랜드 미술관에 소장되어 있습니다.","themes":["꽃과 사물"],"artist_ids":["odilon-redon"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":566,"image_height":900,"image_bytes":163981,"sha256":"dfe970ac9d9cd6514a31b89ec17a27d2a4d8e5ae44fe7df488e7ca62feebf90c","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"파스텔","dimensions_ko":"종이: 84.1 × 58 cm"},{"id":"cma-109138","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"Melancholy","artist":"Odilon Redon (French, 1840–1916)","date":"c. 1868","medium":"graphite on beige wove paper","dimensions":"Sheet: 32.1 x 22 cm (12 5/8 x 8 11/16 in.)","culture":"France, 19th century","accession":"1927.299","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1927.299","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/109138","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1927.299/1927.299_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1927.299/1927.299_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"멜랑콜리","description":"고개를 숙인 여인을 거친 산악 풍경과 함께 그린 드로잉입니다. 르동은 고향 근처 피레네산맥의 이미지를 반복해 고독과 고립의 감정을 표현했고, 이 화면의 그림자 속에는 환상적인 작은 형상도 숨겨 두었습니다.","themes":["인물과 일상","풍경과 빛"],"artist_ids":["odilon-redon"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":691,"image_height":893,"image_bytes":433175,"sha256":"d2434cfaca0b9d2b488a35212c35568f0265b435f7fe9e13f117f2d683d6665d","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"베이지색 평직지에 흑연","dimensions_ko":"종이: 32.1 × 22 cm"},{"id":"cma-115067","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"Vase of Flowers","artist":"Odilon Redon (French, 1840–1916)","date":"c. 1905","medium":"oil on fabric","dimensions":"Framed: 90.8 x 62.2 x 10.2 cm (35 3/4 x 24 1/2 x 4 in.); Unframed: 73 x 59 cm (28 3/4 x 23 1/4 in.)","culture":"France, late 19th-early 20th Century","accession":"1935.233","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1935.233","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/115067","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1935.233/1935.233_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1935.233/1935.233_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"꽃병 — 유채","description":"르동의 후기 작업에서 중요한 비중을 차지한 꽃 정물입니다. 식물학자 아르망 클라보와의 교류로 깊어진 꽃에 대한 관심을 바탕으로, 관찰한 식물의 형태를 꿈에서 본 듯한 색채와 분위기로 바꾸었습니다.","themes":["꽃과 사물"],"artist_ids":["odilon-redon"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":657,"image_height":893,"image_bytes":560470,"sha256":"2a5683f8c1eb79c7f9f260455fa93482ed138ba1cd8b5000b5636fd4c05497d9","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"직물에 유채","dimensions_ko":"액자 포함: 90.8 × 62.2 × 10.2 cm; 액자 제외: 73 × 59 cm"},{"id":"cma-135706","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"Christ Crucified Between the Two Thieves: 'The Three Crosses'","artist":"Rembrandt van Rijn (Dutch, 1606–1669)","date":"1653-c.1660","medium":"drypoint","dimensions":"Sheet: 37.5 x 44 cm (14 3/4 x 17 5/16 in.)","culture":"Rembrandt, 17th century","accession":"1959.241","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1959.241","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/135706","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1959.241/1959.241_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1959.241/1959.241_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"세 십자가","description":"두 도둑 사이에 십자가형을 당하는 그리스도를 드라이포인트로 표현했습니다. 이 인쇄본은 판을 다시 손본 네 번째 상태로, 강한 사선과 인쇄판에 남긴 잉크가 주변을 어둡게 하고 중앙 인물에 빛을 집중시킵니다.","themes":["신화와 상상"],"artist_ids":["rembrandt-van-rijn"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":900,"image_height":764,"image_bytes":337902,"sha256":"3e976934b22e6782f3516a0ee8e93ed311e7097faf9e7c61c968b8997b31724e","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"드라이포인트","dimensions_ko":"종이: 37.5 × 44 cm"},{"id":"cma-144844","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"Tobias Healing His Father's Blindness","artist":"Rembrandt van Rijn (Dutch, 1606–1669)","date":"c. 1640–45","medium":"Pen and brown ink, touched with white gouache; framing lines in pen and brown ink","dimensions":"Sheet: 21.1 x 17.7 cm (8 5/16 x 6 15/16 in.)","culture":"Netherlands","accession":"1969.69","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1969.69","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/144844","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1969.69/1969.69_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1969.69/1969.69_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"아버지의 눈을 치료하는 토비아스","description":"성서 외경 《토비트기》의 눈을 치료하는 장면을 가족의 일상처럼 표현한 드로잉입니다. 미술관은 토비아스의 수술 도구와 안경을 쓴 인물 같은 관찰의 세부가 전통적인 성서 이야기를 새롭게 만든다고 설명합니다.","themes":["인물과 일상","신화와 상상"],"artist_ids":["rembrandt-van-rijn"],"artist_status":"identified","image_width":758,"image_height":900,"image_bytes":441853,"sha256":"b585f031c9a4a5ee91984ea97d6fbd3dce4e49c5720a7be35c4d3f8a9bf09661","collected_at":"2026-10-12T23:50:32.661Z","title_ko_status":"working_translation","themes_status":"editorial_classification","medium_ko":"펜과 갈색 잉크, 흰색 과슈; 펜과 갈색 잉크로 테두리선","dimensions_ko":"종이: 21.1 × 17.7 cm"},{"id":"cma-149378","museum":"The Cleveland Museum of Art","title":"Shah Jahan","artist":"Rembrandt van Rijn (Dutch, 1606–1669)","date":"c. 1656–61","medium":"pen and brown ink and brush and brown wash","dimensions":"Sheet: 22.5 x 17.1 cm (8 7/8 x 6 3/4 in.); Secondary Support: 27.6 x 22.4 cm (10 7/8 x 8 13/16 in.)","culture":"Netherlands","accession":"1978.38","source_url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1978.38","api_url":"https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/149378","image_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1978.38/1978.38_print.jpg","preview_url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1978.38/1978.38_web.jpg","license":"CC0","license_evidence":{"share_license_status":"CC0"},"policy_url":"https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access","title_ko":"샤 자한","description":"무굴 제국의 황제 샤 자한을 그린 드로잉으로, 렘브란트가 인도의 세밀화를 참고해 제작한 작업 가운데 하나입니다. 세밀한 펜 선과 엷은 갈색 잉크의 명암을 결합하고 머리 위의 종이를 긁어 후광 모양을 만들었습니다.","themes":["인물과 일상"],"artist_ids":["rembrandt-van-rijn"],"artist_status":"identified","imag